message: "If you use or discuss this work, please cite this release."
title: "The Scheduled Transformer: A Hypothesis of Depth-Indexed State Regimes in Pre-RMSNorm Language Models"
type: article
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-22
authors:
  - family-names: "Patzer"
    given-names: "Dustin"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
# identifiers:
#   - type: doi
#     value: "10.xxxx/xxxxx"
# repository-code: "https://github.com/USERNAME/scheduled-transformer-hypothesis"
abstract: >-
  The Scheduled Transformer hypothesis proposes that modern pre-normalized
  transformer language models traverse a reproducible, ordered sequence of
  depth-indexed state regimes. Preliminary primary-data analyses strongly
  support structured residual-stream scheduling beyond simple monotonic norm
  growth. This release states the hypothesis and pre-specifies a confirmatory
  empirical program based on full token-level residual-state extraction.
keywords:
  - transformers
  - residual stream
  - representation geometry
  - interpretability
  - depth
  - language models
